<section class="section-tight rule-top" aria-label="Facts">
  <div class="wrap">
    <dl class="rows">
      <div>
        <dt>Who</dt>
        <dd>Freeland Marketing is a remote growth agency for founder-led DTC brands. Legal name: Freeland Marketing and Entertainment, LLC. Founder: <a href="/about/">Kevin Freeland</a>.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>What</dt>
        <dd>Kevin Freeland starts from a brand's public store and ads plus its application answers, reviews accounts more deeply with view-only access, and puts the fixes in order. A system then runs the repeat work: daily ad checks across Meta, Google, Bing and TikTok, landing pages price-checked against checkout, sales date-gated across the site and ads, creator and affiliate programs, retention flows, and AI phone agents. A person handles the exceptions.</dd>
      </div>
<div><dt>Services</dt><dd><a href="/services/meta-ads/">Meta ads</a>, <a href="/services/google-ads-management/">Google Ads</a>, <a href="/services/website-design/">landing pages and CRO</a>, <a href="/services/ai-automation/">AI agents and automation</a>, <a href="/services/email-marketing-automation/">retention and email</a>, <a href="/services/influencer-affiliate/">creator and affiliate programs</a>, <a href="/services/seo/">SEO and AEO</a> and <a href="/services/social-media-management/">organic social systems</a>. One-line answers for each are in <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Brands</dt><dd>Freeland runs systems for two supplement brands today: Mara Labs and Redd Remedies. See <a href="/for/supplement-brands/">supplement brands</a>.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Not for</dt><dd>Pre-launch ideas or brands seeking the cheapest vendor.</dd></div>

      <div>
        <dt>For whom</dt>
        <dd>Founder-led DTC brands that already sell online. Agencies can apply for a white-label partnership on the <a href="/partners/">partners page</a>.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Where</dt>
        <dd>Serves brands nationwide in the United States.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>How to start</dt>
        <dd>Apply for the free <a href="/growth-roadmap/" data-cta="llm_roadmap">Growth Roadmap</a>. More answers are in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The brand applies with five answers. {% if funnel.bookingUrl %}After applying, the brand owner picks a time for a 30-minute call with Kevin.{% else %}After applying, Kevin replies by email to set a 30-minute call.{% endif %} On the call, Kevin walks the owner through the roadmap. The brand then decides whether Freeland does the work or the brand does it itself, and keeps the roadmap either way.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>How it works</dt>
        <dd>Three steps: the Growth Roadmap, walked through on the call; then, if the brand wants Freeland to do the work, Freeland runs the fixes; then the system keeps running. Details are on <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a>.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Cost</dt>
        <dd>Work is scoped after the roadmap, based on what the brand's numbers need. There are no published packages.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Proof</dt>
        <dd>Client results and selected Google reviews are on the <a href="/results/">results page</a>. Each result states what was measured and who reported it: Freeland's internal case records or the client's own letter.</dd>
      </div>
<div><dt>Reviews</dt><dd>Rated 5.0 on Google from 14 reviews as of November 19, 2026. <a href="https://www.google.com/maps?cid=12454933700455021390">See the Google profile</a>.</dd></div>

